    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `summarize_ticket` in `app/summary.py`. A quick check with a fake chat model returned a plain, trimmed `str`, and `pytest -q` passes (2 tests). Neither existing test calls `summarize_ticket`, so that quick check is the only one that exercises it.\n\n```python\ndef summarize_ticket(chat: BaseChatModel, ticket: Ticket) -> str:\n    \"\"\"A one-line summary of `ticket`; generation stops at the first blank line.\"\"\"\n    messages = [SystemMessage(content=SUMMARY_PROMPT), HumanMessage(content=ticket_text(ticket))]\n    reply = chat.invoke(messages, stop=[\"\\n\\n\"])\n    return str(reply.text).strip()\n```\n\n- **One request:** it makes a single `invoke` call with a system message and a user message.\n- **Stop sequence:** `stop=[\"\\n\\n\"]` is passed through `invoke`, so it works the same for any chat model.\n- **Plain string:** it reads the reply with `.text` rather than `str(reply.content)`. Some chat models return content as a list of blocks; `str(reply.content)` would give you that list's printed form, while `.text` joins just the text parts. `.text` returns a subclass of `str`, so I wrap it in `str()` to return a plain string.\n\n**API lookup:** CLAUDE.md asks for a Context7 lookup first, but Context7's monthly quota had run out. Instead, I checked the `invoke` signature and `.text` directly in the installed langchain-core 1.6.5 source in `.venv`.\n\n**Leftover file:** my check script `_chk.py` is still in the project root. Deleting it needed approval, so it's still there and you can delete it."
